--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -22,6 +22,15 @@ go test ./...
 | PATCH | `/projects/{pid}/tasks/{tid}` | `{"title"?,"status"?,"assignee"?}` → 200 |
 | DELETE | `/projects/{pid}/tasks/{tid}` | → 204 |
 
+| POST | `/orgs/{orgID}/users/{uid}/transfer` | `{"toOrgId"}` → 200 `{"id","orgId"}` |
+
+Transfer (moving a user between group companies): only an org admin of `{orgID}`
+may call it, and `{uid}` must currently belong to `{orgID}`. Order of checks: 401
+unknown caller; 404 caller not in `{orgID}`; 403 caller not an org admin; 404 user
+not in `{orgID}`; 400 `toOrgId` missing, equal to `{orgID}`, or not an existing
+organization. On success the user's project memberships (all in the old org) are
+removed, their tasks become unassigned, and they are no longer an org admin.
+
 Statuses: `open`, `doing`, `done`. Errors are `{"error":"..."}`.
 
 ## Access rules
